    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.08<35\\%<0.\\dot{6}<110\\%<1\\frac{1}{4}<\\frac{5}{2}$. Use a scale from $0$ to $3$; positions are shown on the number line.",
      "worked": "Convert to decimal form:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{2}&=2.5\\\\35\\%&=0.35\\\\1\\frac{1}{4}&=1.25\\\\110\\%&=1.1\\end{align*}$$\nThe other two numbers are already decimals. Order by place value:\n$$0.08<0.35<0.666\\ldots<1.1<1.25<2.5.$$\nRewrite in the original forms:\n$$0.08<35\\%<0.\\dot{6}<110\\%<1\\frac{1}{4}<\\frac{5}{2}.$$\nUse a scale from $0$ to $3$ and place each value at its corresponding decimal position, as shown.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
          "id": "v2-5458e-p51-practice-slot-30-slot-30-solution-number-line",
          "role": "solution",
          "format": "tikz",
